Figure 6.1: Number of participants by neighborhood in New York City
MPX NYC participants reflect a vivid cross-section of queer and trans New York. They lived in familiar queer neighborhoods—from Hell’s Kitchen to Bedford-Stuy—and brought with them diverse experiences of health, identity, and connection. This section paints a portrait of who they were and how they were connected.

Codemake_tabledata_gatherings &lt;- function(){
  targets::tar_read(data_bipartite_graph_collected) |&gt;
    tidygraph::activate(edges)|&gt;
    data.frame() |&gt;
    dplyr::group_by(place_borough, place_community, place_neighborhood) |&gt;
    dplyr::summarize(count = dplyr::n()) |&gt;
    dplyr::rename(borough = place_borough, community = place_community, neighborhood = place_neighborhood) |&gt;
    dplyr::arrange(-count) |&gt;
    dplyr::ungroup() |&gt;
    dplyr::filter(!is.na(borough)) |&gt;
    dplyr::mutate(proportion = count / sum(count))
}


scale_labels &lt;- c("0", "1-10", "11-20", "21-30", "31+")

